# Capacitor-ready frontend (Ionic UI later)

Capacitor wraps this Vite React app in a native WebView. Do not add Ionic UI components yet. Keep one React codebase.

- **Pages stay self-contained.** One screen per route; logic in hooks. App chrome (header + left menu) lives in `AppLayout`, not in each page.
- **Navigation:** keep `react-router-dom`. Prefer `Link` / `useNavigate` over `window.location` (except a last-resort auth bounce). The left menu is a split pane on wide screens and an overlay drawer on small ones — that maps to Ionic `IonSplitPane` + `IonMenu` if we adopt Ionic later.
- **API:** keep `fetch` behind `api.js`. Web uses same-origin `/api`. Native builds set `VITE_API_BASE` (see `.env.android.example`) to `https://api.zipdeck.app`. Do not scatter absolute URLs in pages. `server.hostname` may be `zipdeck.app` for password autofill. Never set it to the API host: Capacitor serves any request matching its own hostname from the bundled assets, so `/api` would return `index.html` with a 200 instead of reaching the server. Do not point `VITE_API_BASE` at `https://zipdeck.app` in native builds. Play-distributed Android Google Sign-In needs an Android OAuth client (same Cloud project as the Web client, package `com.zipdeck.app`) for **every** Play App signing SHA-1 — hybrid signing uses more than one. Do not put Android client IDs in `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`. `[16] Account reauth failed` after the account picker means a Play cert is missing in Cloud, not a bad AAB. See README “Android (Capacitor)”.
- **Dialogs:** do not add new `window.prompt`, `window.confirm`, or `window.alert`. Use in-app modals/forms (existing confirms can stay until touched).
- **Pointers:** every action must work with tap, not hover-only. Hover is extra, never the only way. Accordion sections open on tap.
- **Inputs:** prefer real `<button>` / `<input>` with ~44px tap targets. File pickers and color inputs stay isolated (Capacitor plugins later).
- **Storage:** keep token access in `api.js` (`localStorage` is fine for now; native can swap to Preferences later).
- **CSS:** prefer flex/grid and CSS variables. Use `--safe-top` / `--safe-bottom` (and `viewport-fit=cover`) instead of `100vh`-only layouts; `100dvh` is the web fallback. No hover-only disclosure.
- **Do not** add PWA-only APIs, browser extensions, or desktop-only drag-and-drop as the sole path for a feature.
